.TH OMATRACK 1 "October 2026" "omatrack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omatrack \- ProTracker-style music tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omatrack
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile.mod\fR]
.br
.B omatrack \-\-render
.I out.wav
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I file.mod
.br
.B omatrack \-\-help
.br
.B omatrack \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omatrack
is a terminal tracker for 31-sample, 4-channel ProTracker modules
.RB ( M.K. ,
.BR M!K! ,
.BR FLT4 ,
and
.BR 4CHN ).
With no
.I file.mod
it starts an empty module.
.PP
The view needs about 76 columns and 20 rows.
Space plays from the cursor.
Enter toggles edit mode.
A
.B *
after the title means the song has unsaved edits.
Quit, new, and open ask before discarding them.
.PP
Colors come from the active Omarchy theme when one is installed, otherwise
from the built-in ProTracker palette.
See
.BR CONFIGURATION .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " \fIname\fR"
.BR auto ,
.BR omarchy ,
.BR protracker ,
.BR phosphor ,
or
.BR terminal .
Overrides the config file.
.B terminal
uses ANSI colors so the terminal's own palette shows through.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Read this config file instead of the default.
.TP
.BR \-\-render " \fIout.wav\fR"
Mix the song to 16-bit stereo WAV and exit.
Does not open an audio device.
.TP
.BR \-\-rate " \fIhz\fR"
Sample rate for
.BR \-\-render .
Default is the config value, or 44100.
.TP
.BR \-\-max-seconds " \fIn\fR"
Stop
.B \-\-render
after
.I n
seconds if the song does not loop.
Default is the config value, or 600.
.TP
.BR \-\-interpolate " \fImode\fR"
.B linear
or
.BR nearest .
.TP
.BR \-\-separation " \fI0\-100\fR"
100 is hard Amiga panning.
0 is mono.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the key list and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Toggle edit mode.
.TP
.B Space
Play or stop.
.TP
.B ?
Key list.
.B Esc
closes it.
.TP
.B Ctrl-F
File menu:
.B n
new,
.B o
open,
.B s
save,
.B a
save as.
.TP
.B Ctrl-S
Save.
An untitled module asks for a path.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Z / Ctrl-Y
Undo / redo.
.TP
.B q, Esc, Ctrl-Q
Quit.
.B q
works from browse mode.
.B Ctrl-Q
works anywhere.
.B Esc
clears a block, then leaves edit mode, then quits.
Each asks when the song is modified.
.TP
.B Ctrl-C
Copy.
It does not quit.
.TP
.B Tab / Shift-Tab
Next or previous pane.
In edit mode, Tab changes channel.
.TP
.B 1 2 3 4
Mute a channel.
In edit mode use
.BR Alt-1 " through " Alt-4 .
.TP
.B F1 / F2
Octave, 1 through 3.
.TP
.B F3 / F4
Edit step, 0 through 16.
.PP
In edit mode the lower piano row is
.B Z S X D C V G B H N J M
and the upper row is
.BR "Q 2 W 3 E R 5 T 6 Y 7 U" .
.B ?
inside the program lists block, order, and sample keys.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default file is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omatrack/config.toml ,
or
.I ~/.config/omatrack/config.toml
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
A missing file uses the defaults.
A file that cannot be parsed is ignored, and the reason is shown on the
status line.
An example is installed at
.IR /usr/share/omatrack/config.toml .
.PP
.EX
theme = "auto"
[audio]
sample_rate = 44100
interpolation = "linear"
stereo_separation = 100
max_seconds = 600
[edit]
octave = 2
step = 1
.EE
.SH THEMES
.B auto
reads the active Omarchy theme.
Current Omarchy writes it to
.I ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme
.RB ( $XDG_STATE_HOME
when that is set).
Older Omarchy used
.IR ~/.config/omarchy/current/theme .
The canonical palette is
.IR colors.toml .
If that file is absent, omatrack reads
.IR alacritty.toml ,
.IR kitty.conf ,
or
.I ghostty.conf
from the same directory.
.PP
.B SIGUSR1
reloads the theme, and so does a change to those files.
Truecolor is used when
.B COLORTERM
is
.I truecolor
or
.IR 24bit ,
or when
.B TERM
names kitty, alacritty, or ghostty.
Otherwise colors are quantized to 256 or 16 ANSI colors.
.B \-\-theme terminal
skips that and uses the terminal palette directly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/omatrack/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme/
Active Omarchy theme on current installs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/omarchy/current/theme/
Active Omarchy theme on older installs.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success, or help or version was printed.
.TP
.B 1
The module, the WAV file, or the terminal could not be used.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was not understood.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The in-program help
.RB ( ? )
and the project README.
